  "dom_id": "question-143338",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.16$ | $0.01$ | $0.03$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.64$ | $0.09$ | $0.07$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $P(X=3,Y=2)=P(X=3)\\cdot P(Y=2)$\n\nII. $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n\nIII. $X$ and $Y$ are independent",
